(
 '* 16.0.0 ⋄ 2026-10-31'
 '  * Breaking change: `Init`, `MakeHTML_Doc` and `ConvertMarkdownFile` no longer change the parameter'
 '    namespace passed to them, so it can be reused for another document. Parameters established by'
 '    `Init` (including embedded ones) are available on `ns.parms`: pass that to `MakeHTML_Doc`.'
 '  * Breaking change: a link in a header is now reported and shown as text. It used to be compiled, although'
 '    the documentation says that this is not possible. Because of the anchor around a header that resulted in'
 '    an `<a>` nested in an `<a>`, which is invalid HTML, and browsers then tear the header apart.'
 '  * TOCs are now narrower in order to emphasize the fact that they might hide parts of the '
 '    document, something that for performance reasons happens after "Hide" and then "Show" again.'
 '    They occupy 75% of the document width, centered.'
 '  * Documentation clarified regarding markdown in HTML blocks.'
 '  * Performance: code-block fences are found with a single search over the whole document instead of'
 '    two regular-expression calls per line, and LeanPub extensions look for code blocks only after a change.'
 '  * Performance: finding the end of a code block and the extent of a table no longer scans the rest of'
 '    the document.'
 '  * Performance: smart typography needs two instead of nine regular-expression calls per paragraph, and'
 '    none at all when there is nothing to replace.'
 '  * Performance: emphasis, images and links are not looked for when their markers do not occur.'
 '  * Performance: header numbers are injected in a single pass over the HTML.'
 '  * Performance: footnotes, link references, definition lists, HTML blocks and paragraphs no longer'
 '    copy or scan the whole document (or the whole HTML) over and over again.'
 '  * Performance: paragraphs no longer compute a code mask that was never used.'
 '  * Closing `#` characters of headers now follow CommonMark: any number of them is removed, provided'
 '    they are separated from the caption by a space; until now they were removed only when their number'
 '    matched the leading `#` characters and the header was not indented.'
 '  * `#` can now be escaped with a backslash, so a caption may end with " \#".'
 '  * The function `EstablishDefaultHomeFolder` was removed: it could never do anything, and it called a'
 '    function `Get_Home` that does not exist.'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * The "Classic" theme defined uppercase captions by accident.'
 '    * A "⎕" was not considered part of a name, so "SE" nd "⎕SE" ended up to be the same.'
 '      Now anything that starts with a "⎕" is considered. Can be important for "⎕SE" in captions'
 '    * The SVG icons of the LeanPub extensions carried the literal text "[title]" as their'
 '      `aria-label`, so screen readers announced "[title]" rather than, say, "Warning".'
 '    * `Matrix2MarkdownTable`: a column header with just a leading ":" (like ":Name") made the'
 '      column right-aligned rather than left-aligned.'
 '    * A "\" at the end of the last line of a paragraph or a list item injected a pointless `<br>`;'
 '      it is now dropped.'
 '    * Abbreviations caused a VALUE ERROR when `syntaxSugar` was 0.'
 '    * Lines starting with "⍝" were removed from code blocks whose fence carried an info string like "~~~ apl".'
 '    * A paragraph with a line starting with "=> " but no "!> " line (so no collapsible) was deleted.'
 '    * A footnote reference in the last header crashed MarkAPL, and references with digits, "_", "∆" or "⍙"'
 '      in auto-link headers went unreported. Footnote ids may contain "∆" and "⍙" (now documented);'
 '      an empty id ("[^]:") is rejected and reported.'
 '    * Abbreviations: a colon in the explanation crashed MarkAPL, and abbreviations with "&" or "+"'
 '      (like "R&D" or "C++") were mangled.'
 '    * An embedded parameter with an invalid name crashed MarkAPL. Invalid names are now reported'
 '      and never executed.'
 '    * Header numbering crashed when a deeper header came before the first header of the top numbered level.'
 '    * A table that could not be processed vanished silently; it is now reported.'
 '    * A code span holding something like "<https://…>" ahead of a real automatic link was turned into a link.'
 '    * Curly braces in the text of a link (like "[dfns {⍵}](…)") destroyed the URL.'
 '    * Smart typography changed URLs: "..." in a link became "…", "--" became "–".'
 '    * Emphasis: a "*", "_" or "__" surrounded by blanks upset the pairing of the other markers,'
 '      and "***x***" and "___x___" produced unclosed tags.'
 '    * Unpaired "==" and "~~" left an unclosed <mark> or <del>, and "==" inside a URL became markup.'
 '    * A "\&" inside code was escaped twice and showed up as "&amp;".'
 '    * A "<" that did not start a tag was not escaped when an automatic link followed later on.'
 '    * Two opening backticks were closed by a single one, making the rest of the paragraph code.'
 '    * RunTestsInBatchMode asked about code coverage, so it could not run unattended.'
 '    * Nested conversions (tables in lists, blockquotes, collapsibles, asides, sub-TOCs) ignored settings'
 '      like `syntaxSugar`, and a blockquote switched `lowercaseID` back on, breaking TOC links.'
 '    * The TOC was badly nested when header levels were skipped (h1 → h3 → h1) or when the first header'
 '      was not the shallowest one: the TOC list got closed too early.'
 '    * SubTOCs were not created for headers with inline markup, picked the wrong chapter for duplicate'
 '      captions, and one SubTOC that could not be created prevented all following ones.'
 '    * Headers with the same caption (like "Examples" in several chapters) were not numbered.'
 '    * Lists: "1)" after a bulleted list, type switches on nested levels, closing order of mixed nested'
 '      lists, wrongly indented paragraphs, a nested list after a table, a line straight after a code block,'
 '      and a list marker left on items with special attributes were all handled wrongly. Warnings about'
 '      tables or blockquotes inside a list got lost.'
 '    * Using a link reference twice: the text of the first link became the title of the second one.'
 '    * A "](" without a matching "[" mangled the paragraph.'
 '    * A blockquote indented by up to three blanks became a nested blockquote.'
 '    * LeanPub extensions: k warnings were reported k² times, and a block on line 1 upset the following'
 '      blocks of the same kind.'
 '    * "__" inside a URL (like Python''s "__init__") was taken as markup.'
 '    * "![" that was not followed by "](" (like "![x] foo") was taken as an image and swallowed text.'
 '    * The link report showed a "%" in a link text as "&".'
 '    * Tables: a row of empty cells was taken as the footer separator (all rows after it ended up in the'
 '      footer) or as the header separator, or it disappeared. It is now an ordinary row.'
 '    * Embedded function calls: a call on a line of its own was executed twice when it returned an empty'
 '      result; several calls in one paragraph garbled the paragraph; an empty result scrambled the text.'
 '    * Embedded function calls with an argument executed a dfn twice: it was tried without the argument'
 '      first. Now it is called once; a dfn that needs a left argument but gets none is reported.'
 '    * An embedded parameter with a non-numeric value for a numeric parameter (like a trailing comment'
 '      in "[parm]:toc=2 ⍝ …") crashed MarkAPL. It is now reported and the default value is kept.'
 '    * "[parm]:" was case sensitive, contrary to the documentation: "[PARM]:" was silently ignored.'
 '    * `bookmarkMayStartWithDigit←0` did not remove leading digits from header IDs, and in a paragraph'
 '      with several links it applied only to the first one, so such links pointed nowhere.'
 '    * Text after a SubTOC directive (like "<<SubTOC>> Some text") vanished without a word. It is now'
 '      reported, and the line is treated as a paragraph.'
 '    * A SubTOC with a user-defined class ("<<SubTOC {.foo}>>") got two "class" attributes; browsers'
 '      ignored the second one, so the SubTOC lost its styling. The class names are now merged.'
 '    * A link reference without a definition ("[][typo]") was not reported, contrary to the documentation.'
 '      It is now reported when `checkLinks` is 1.'
 '    * A short bookmark link ("[Some head](#)") to a header with a custom ID ("{#xyz}") pointed to'
 '      "#some-head" rather than to "#xyz", and was reported as invalid.'
 '    * `[data]:` kept all definitions of a name, although the documentation says that the last one wins,'
 '      and accepted any name. A second definition now causes a warning. A name must start with an ASCII letter'
 '      or an underscore and may otherwise contain ASCII letters, digits and underscores; anything else is reported.'
 '    * `Matrix2MarkdownList` checked the list type of the first row instead of its nesting level: an ordered list'
 '      could not start at anything but 1 in the first row, while any nesting level was accepted there. It also'
 '      rejected list types above 999, and reported an invalid list type as "must have 3 columns".'
 '    * With `checkFootnotes` being 1 a footnote reference without an ID ("[^]") caused a warning with nothing'
 '      after the colon; it now says what is wrong. A "[^" without a closing "]" is no longer reported as a footnote:'
 '      the warning showed the HTML that followed it, like "</p>".'
 '    * The documentation claimed that a header cannot contain an image, but it can.'
 '    * The "Dark" theme did not hide `.hide` when printing, unlike "Classic" and "Modern". The documentation'
 '      now says that `.hide` works on screen and in print; for "show in print only" use `.print_only`.'
 '    * An escaped double quote (`\"`) kept its `\` when it was the only double quote (plus a pointless warning),'
 '      and always when `syntaxSugar` was 0; then even a single unescaped double quote came out as `\"`.'
 '    * `Matrix2MarkdownTable` escaped `|` only for some numbers of cells holding one; otherwise none was escaped,'
 '      resulting in rows with too many columns.'
 '    * Numerous corrections and additions to the documentation; `MarkAPL` needs at least Dyalog 18.2, not 18.0.'
 '    * The warning "odd number of double quotes" reported a line number that was one too low, except in a blockquote.'
 '      All other warnings from inside a blockquote were one too high. A nested blockquote and a table or blockquote'
 '      in a list item ignored the line number of what contains them.'
 '* 15.0.0 ⋄ 2026-07-18'
 '  * Two new style sheets added: "Modern" and "Classic".'
 '  * " ==mark this== " is now converted into " <mark>mark this</mark> ". '
 '  * The "Dark_screen" style sheet got improved.             '
 '  * All three style sheets behave well on mobiles and tablets now.'
 '  * All printing style sheets got improved.                            '
 '  * Retired: the style sheets "BlackAndWhite" and "MarkAPL".'
 '  * A document "Test-Themes" got added. '
 '* 14.2.0 ⋄ 2025-08-24'
 '  * Bug fix: `GetCommandLineParms` stumbled over empty settings like `RIDE_INIT=`'
 '  * Packages updated'
 '* 14.1.0 ⋄ 2025-05-12'
 '  * Package `FilesAndDirs` updated'
 '* 14.0.0 ⋄ 2025-04-04'
 '  * Potentially breaking change: `Version` now returns a har vector stemming from the package config file.'
 '  * Dependencies updated'
 '* 13.1.0 ⋄ 2024-09-26'
 '  * In earlier version when a collapsible was expanded, all other collapsibles were contracted.'
 '    This was not welcomed for users in need for comparing the content of two collapsibles.'
 '  * A url like "foo,htnl" in a link was always changed to "https://foo.html" - that''s wrong.'
 '* 13.0.0 ⋄ 2024-08-09'
 '  * Syntax changed for marking up checkboxes in Markdown: `- [ ]` or `- [x]` respectively. '
 '    This is the reason why this is a new major version.\\'
 '    This brings MarkAPL in line with the GitHub syntax which is now well established.\\'
 '  * CSS for all lists in all CSS files updated for both screen and print'
 '  * Deprecated `collapsibleTOC` removed'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * Both flavours of lists as well as check boxes were wrongly displayed when part of a blockquote'
 '    * ID assigned to an ambiguous header in MarkAPL.md'
 '    * Documentation corrected regarding check boxes (the documentation stated that a `<div>` was put'
 '      around the list, but that''s is not the case)'
 '    * Sometimes a caption did not get a number assigned (#45)'
 '    * Insufficient white space between cited paragraphs in the "Dark" theme''s "print" SS. (#44)'
 '* 12.1.2 ⋄ 2024-04-07'
 '  * `Help` did not work when `MarkAPL` was brought into the WS with `]Tatin.LoadPackages`'
 '* 12.1.1 ⋄ 2024-01-29'
 '  * Bug fixes      '
 '    * The print style sheet produced a way too big basic font size.'
 '    * `CreateParms` called `FilesAndDirs` but should call function `F` instead.'
 '* 12.1.0 ⋄ 2024-01-11'
 '  * New parameters `tocShowCaption` and `tocHideCaption` introduced for replacing the default captions of'
 '    the "Copy"/"Hide" button in the TOC area.'
 '  * New parameter `startHeaderNoWith` allows specifying the initial value of the level-1 header number.'
 '  * New parameters `copyCaption` and `copiedCaption` introduced for replacing the default captions of the '
 '    "Copy" button in code blocks.'
 '  * Restriction removed from `ConvertMarkdownFile`: allows specification of `inputFilename` now.'
 '  * Print styles improved.'
 '  * Table styling improved.'
 '  * Bug fixes:'
 '    * `cssURL` was not correctly processed when not set.'
 '* 12.0.2 ⋄ 2023-12-15'
 '  * Bug fixes:'
 '    * Function `Version` addressed `TatinVars` incorrectly; introduced with 12.0.1'
 '* 12.0.1 ⋄ 2023-12-14'
 '  * Bug fixes: '
 '    * The CSS variables in the "Dark" theme weren''t interpreted by the IE via the OCX control.'
 '    * Guillemets were not processed when found at the beginning of a paragraph.'
 '    * `collapsibleTOC` was rejected when defined as an embedded parameter. Not processed anymore, but'
 '      should be ignored rather than rejected.'
 '* 12.0.0 ⋄ 2023-12-11'
 '  * BREAKING CHANGES: '
 '    * HTML tags in Markdown are now left alone, implementing the original intention, and bringing MarkAPL '
 '      in line with big shots like GitHub Markdown                   '
 '    * The `id` parameter as well as `href` in case they point to an internal anchor (`#`) are now by'
 '      default lowercased. You can change that by setting the new parameter `lowercaseID←1`'
 '  * Collapsibles implemented with the `<details>` and `<summary>` tags.'
 '  * Accordions (multiple collapsibles in succession) implemented.'
 '  * Check boxes (ticked and un-ticked) added.'
 '  * Code blocks now offer a Copy-to-clipboard" button.'
 '  * The main TOC now always has a button "Show/Hide" that toggles the TOC when clicked.'
 '  * New parameter `copy2ClipboardBtn` (defaults to 1) can be used to suppress the new copy-to-clipboard button '
 '    for all code blocks.'
 '  * New parameter `javaScript` (defaults to 1) can be used to suppress the injection of **any* JavaScript '
 '    code. '
 '  * New "Dark" theme established as the new default layout.'
 '  * The LeanPub icons are now SVGs injected into the document, so no Internet connection is required anymore'
 '    when LeanPub extensions are used.'
 '  * The "normalization" part of the screen has been updated from 7.0 to 8.0.1'
 '  * The parameters `collapsibleTOC` and `showHide` have been retired.'
 '  * The special MarkAPL feature `<<br>>` has been retired: now `<br>` will do'
 '  * All CSS layouts improved (again).'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * Some CSS files were ANSI encoded when they must be UTF8-encoded.'
 '    * `ignoreEmbeddedParms←1` did not remove embedded parameters from the input.'
 '    * Links in footnotes were not processed in case <<br>> was not part of the footprint '
 '    * The LeanPub extension "Tip" was not implemented by accident.'
 '    * The link list (print only) showed the URL followed by the link text - should have been the other way round  '
 '* 11.1.0 ⋄ 2023-08-13'
 '  * Layout `MarkAPL_screen` improved (TOC and inline code)'
 '  * Layout `BlackOnWhite_screen` improved (TOC and inline code)'
 '  * Documentation improved / updated'
 '  * `LICENSE` updated'
 '  * Bug fix: a header like `## This header contains two ## ##` was not handled correctly'
 '  * Packages updated'
 '  * `Make` updated'
 '  * Internal change: class script replaced by functions, operators and variables'
 '* 11.0.5 ⋄ 2022-06-15'
 '  * Bug fix: `Matrix2MarkdownList` complained wrongly that ⍵ should have 2 columns: 3 is correct'
 '* 11.0.4 ⋄ 2022-10-26'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * `ShowHtml` did not cope when the right argument pointed to the current directory'
 '* 11.0.3 ⋄ 2022-05-09'
 '  * Bug fixes:'
 '    * When the command line of the current instance of Dyalog contained something like'
 '      lx="1 #.RunThis 1"'
 '      then that expression was subject to ⍎, meaning the function got executed.'
 '    * URL links with APL code in the link text were buggy'
 '* 11.0.2 ⋄ 2021-10-12'
 '  * Two successive lists were indistinguishable from a single one in all the CSS.'
 '  * Tatin packages updated'
 '  * Internal change: now managed by Cider rather than acre'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * MarkAPL 11 relied on the variable TatinVars'
 '    * Two successive lists were not distinguishable. This was a CSS problem; changed.'
 '* 11.0.1'
 '  Bug reports:'
 '  * Internal link in a LeanPub block were wrongly reported as invalid no matter what'
 '  * Footnotes that were not referenced were not displayed. They are now displayed but a warning is reported'
 '* 11.0.0'
 '  * HTML and CSS but also Markdown documents (though only in develoment mode, read as part of the project'
 '    rather than the package "MarkAPL" now always live in a sub folder Files/.'
 '  * Both the project and the package require a variable `TatinVars.HOME`. While this variable always exists'
 '    for the MarkAPL package (because its a Tatin convention) it needs to be injected for the project.'
 ''
 'For information regarding older versions see <https://github.com/aplteam/MarkAPL/releases>'
 '                                 '
)
